[ChapterName "1. b4 e6 2. Bb2 Nf6 - Main line"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/fObXM70G/aVCMxBP2"]
[Annotator "https://lichess.org/@/Bijbrengen"]
[UTCDate "2021.02.07"]
[UTCTime "08:52:24"]

1. b4 { This is the move that indicates the Polish opening or Orang Oetan or Sokolsky. } 1... e6 { The best respons for black. Attacking the pawn on b4 without being counter attacked on e5 after Bb2. Black still takes the opportunity to attack some space in the centre instead of grabbing it with e5. } 2. Bb2 { Strangely enough rejecting the pawn offer is preferable for black because development seems more relevant than an important pawn. } 2... Nf6 3. a3 { Defending b4. } 3... b6 { The beste move for black. Opening the diagonal a8 - h1 for the black bishop and preventing c5 when black starts building up his pawn structure. } 4. e3 { Opening the diagonal for the white bishop and building up a pawn structure from f2 up to c5. To prevent this black has already played b6. } 4... c5 { Black attacks the pawn structure of black. } 5. b5 d5 6. Nf3 { Also c4 is possible if white wants to start attacking the black defenses right away. } *


